<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Jacket</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1750–<a href="/years/1830">1830</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sagoyewatha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Red Jacket, or Sagoyewatha, was a Seneca orator and chief of the Wolf clan. Named for the red coat he wore as a British ally in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a>, he became the leading Seneca spokesman in dealings with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, negotiating over land and defending Seneca religion and customs against missionaries in celebrated speeches.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-jacket.jpg" alt="Red Jacket" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chromolithograph by Corbould from a painting by C.B. King; printed by C. Hallmandel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_Jacket_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
